   "notes": "The dataset preserves the workbook's full numeric precision, normalized to 12 significant digits. Asterisks are represented by b8_observation=detected_one_peak_no_volume; dagger marks are represented by b1_observation=rhombohedrally_distorted_detected_no_volume; double-dagger rows retain the measured B8 values but leave their unconstrained uncertainties blank. The supplement labels all numeric error columns generically with +/- and does not define a statistic, so they are recorded as published uncertainties.",
